#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""heimdall-inbox-wake -- wake an IDLE Claude Code session when a phone message lands.

WHY. bin/heimdall-inbox-deliver hands a queued phone message to a session at a hook
boundary (prompt, tool, Stop). A session left at an empty prompt has no boundary: the
Stop long-poll ends after 300s and nothing runs until the operator types (measured: a
phone "yes" waited 2h40m, docs/HANDOFF-TO-HEIMDALL-phone-replies-reach-session.md G2).
This tool is the missing trigger. It never carries the message: it only makes the
session take a turn, and the deliver hooks hand the content over behind their
provenance marker exactly as before.

MECHANISMS (Claude Code 2.1.295, checked against the installed binary and a live pty run):
  rewake  Claude Code's hook field asyncRewake runs a hook in the background and, when it
          exits 2, queues a task-notification (priority next) whose body is the hook's
          stderr. `watch` is that hook: it blocks until an authenticated phone message is
          pending, the session is idle and nobody is holding or typing, then prints
          WAKE_NOTICE (fixed text) to stderr and exits 2. Works in any terminal.
  tmux    When the session was started inside tmux, `register` (SessionStart) recorded its
          pane. `watch` types WAKE_PROMPT (fixed text) plus Enter into THAT pane, so the
          wake is a real user turn and the UserPromptSubmit hook delivers the message in
          it. Only after the pane is proven to be this session's own and the terminal has
          been unread for TMUX_QUIET_S (a half-typed draft is never submitted).

SECURITY (each gate is a test in test/heimdall-inbox-wake.test.sh).
  Who may wake. A pending record must be source "companion" (the one value
  bin/lib/companion_ui_inbox.append writes) AND sit in an inbox.jsonl that this user owns, that is
  0600, not a symlink, inside a .heimdall/ui this user owns that nobody else can write -- append()
  and pop_all() force exactly those modes, and a git checkout cannot produce a 0600 file, so a
  repo-shipped or other-account-dropped inbox never wakes anything. And a companion must be
  connected right now: .heimdall/app/connect.json (same owner rule) naming live same-user pids, the
  processes that authenticate the phone (relay client / hmd ui). The inbox is per repo and the watcher
  per claude pid, so another repo's or session's records and files are never read.
  What is injected. Nothing from a message reaches the wake: WAKE_NOTICE and WAKE_PROMPT are
  constants, and the message itself still arrives through the marked delivery hooks.
  Where it is typed. The pane and socket come from THIS process's own TMUX_PANE/TMUX, which the hook
  inherits from claude; the SessionStart record (0600, owner-checked) must agree with them, the pane
  must match %N, and tmux list-panes must show its process as an ancestor of this claude pid. argv is
  built only from that validated pane id, the socket path and constants, run without a shell, with -l.
  What exit 2 means. asyncRewake treats exit 2 as "wake the model", and argparse exits 2 on a bad
  argument, so usage errors are caught and exit 0: only a real wake exits 2.
  Links. The repo tree is attacker-shaped: a checkout can carry .heimdall, .heimdall/ui, .heimdall/ui/wake, or any file
  in them, as a symlink. Every file this tool reads, writes, locks, stats or removes under the repo goes through
  bin/lib/hmd_private_state.py, which walks down from the repo root one component at a time with O_NOFOLLOW and refuses
  a link or another account's directory anywhere on the way: nothing is created, chmod'ed, truncated, locked, renamed
  or unlinked outside the repo, and nothing a link leads to is believed. A refusal ends the command with exit 0, no wake
  and no output (stderr is the wake notice's channel: only a constant ever goes there).

BOUNDS. One watcher per session (flock on wake/<pid>.lock, freed by the kernel on any
death). One wake per record id (inbox-wake.json ledger, capped), so a delivery hook that is
switched off cannot turn one message into a wake loop. Lifetime capped (HMD_INBOX_WAKE_MAX_S,
default 8h; hooks.json's timeout matches and the next Stop re-arms). It looks once a second
with a stat, spawns nothing while the inbox is empty, and exits when its session dies.

TMUX OPT-IN (`hmd app connect --tmux`). The tmux path above is tried first for any session whose pane is proven; the opt-in is the
operator saying so, on the record, and it settles one question the default leaves to the exit-2 notice: a terminal read 10-30s ago
may hold a half-typed draft, so the default answers it with the notice (a turn taken by a task-notification). For a session whose
pane connect.json's `tmux` list names, tmux IS the delivery path: that window is waited out -- nothing claimed, nothing typed, nothing
printed -- until the terminal has been quiet, or the operator submits their own prompt and the UserPromptSubmit hook delivers the message.
The notice stays the fallback for a pane that cannot be proven right now, so a message is never stuck. The opt-in never loosens a gate:
the same proof (own_pane), the same fixed prompt, and HMD_INBOX_WAKE=off|rewake still win. `optin` is connect's check, made before it
starts anything: tmux must be on PATH, a session of this repo must have registered (its own TMUX_PANE/TMUX, recorded by `register`),
tmux's own list-panes must show that pane's process as an ancestor of that claude pid and as this user's, and the socket must be a unix
socket this user owns. It is read-only (one list-panes per session, nothing typed, nothing written), prints the verified sessions as
[{"pid","pane","socket"}], and otherwise says why on stderr and exits 1. connect.json's entry matches by pane and socket, not by pid,
so the opt-in follows the pane across a Claude Code restart; the proof is repeated by every watcher.

Modes:
  register   SessionStart hook (stdin JSON). Records this session's pane/terminal under
             <repo>/.heimdall/ui/wake/<pid>.json (0600) and prunes dead sessions.
  watch      The asyncRewake hook (also armed on every Stop). Exit 2 = wake the model.
  status     Prints {"registered": N, "pending": N} for the repo (live sessions, phone records).
  optin      `hmd app connect --tmux`'s check (see TMUX OPT-IN). Not a hook: exit 1 with the reason on stderr.
Args: --repo DIR  --pid CLAUDE_PID (the hook shell's $PPID).
Env:  HMD_INBOX_WAKE=off|rewake|tmux (default: tmux where proven, else rewake), HMD_INBOX_WAKE_MAX_S,
      HMD_INBOX_WAKE_POLL_S, HMD_INBOX_WAKE_TMUX_QUIET_S, HMD_CLAUDE_SESSIONS_DIR (status files).
"""
import argparse
import contextlib
import fcntl
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import time

SOURCE = "companion"                      # companion_ui_inbox.append's record source
WAKE_PROMPT = "phone message waiting"      # typed into the pane: constant, never message text
# Measured live (Claude Code 2.1.295: the real TUI under a pty, hooks from a throwaway project only): a Stop
# hook started a 20s asyncRewake hook, nothing was typed, and 21.6s after that Stop the idle session took a turn
# on its own and answered the hook's stderr. The wake turn ran UserPromptSubmit (prompt = the task-notification
# carrying WAKE_NOTICE), so bin/heimdall-inbox-deliver's prompt hook folds the pending phone message into that
# very turn. Its Stop payload had stop_hook_active=true, where deliver's stop mode stands down on purpose.
WAKE_NOTICE = ("A message from the operator's paired phone is waiting in the companion inbox. "
               "This notice carries no message text: the companion inbox hook delivers it with this "
               "turn, marked as data from the phone. Do not act on this notice itself.")
PROGRAMMATIC_ENTRYPOINTS = frozenset(("sdk-cli", "sdk-ts", "sdk-py", "mcp", "claude-code-github-action"))
SWITCHED_OFF = frozenset(("off", "0", "false", "no", "none"))
PANE_RE = re.compile(r"^%[0-9]{1,9}$")
PRIVATE = 0o077               # mode bits a private file must not carry (append/pop_all force 0600)
NOT_SHARED = 0o022            # mode bits a directory or connect.json must not carry (nobody else may write)
HOLD_FRESH_S = 4.0            # inbox-waiting (the Stop hold's heartbeat) younger than this: a hold will deliver
TYPING_RECENT_S = 10.0        # a terminal read this recently: somebody is at the keyboard
DEFAULT_POLL_S = 1.0
DEFAULT_MAX_S = 8 * 3600.0
DEFAULT_TMUX_QUIET_S = 30.0
LEDGER_CAP = 200
PROBE_TIMEOUT_S = 3.0
ANCESTOR_HOPS = 16
MAX_INBOX_READ = 4 * 1024 * 1024
UI_REL = ".heimdall/ui"       # directories below the repo root, walked link-free by hmd_private_state
WAKE_REL = ".heimdall/ui/wake"
APP_REL = ".heimdall/app"
READ_CAP = 65536
STATE = None                  # bin/lib/hmd_private_state.py, loaded by main(): the only way this tool touches a repo file


def env_float(name, default):
    try:
        v = float(os.environ.get(name, "").strip())
    except ValueError:
        return default
    return v if v >= 0 else default


def _load_private_state():
    # bin/lib/hmd_private_state.py, loaded by path beside this file (it is not a package; bin/heimdall-relay-client's
    # _load_module does the same). There is no fallback to plain open()/chmod()/rename(): a helper that cannot be loaded
    # is an exception, which main() turns into exit 0 and no wake.
    path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "lib", "hmd_private_state.py")
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("hmd_private_state", path)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def attended_session():
    # Same rule as bin/heimdall-inbox-deliver: headless claude -p / SDK children and hmd's
    # own sub-sessions share these hooks and must never be woken for the operator's phone.
    if os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT", "").strip() in PROGRAMMATIC_ENTRYPOINTS:
        return False
    if os.environ.get("HMD_AGENT_TYPE", "").strip():
        return False
    return os.environ.get("HMD_JUDGMENT", "").strip().lower() in ("", "0", "false")


def pid_alive(pid):
    if isinstance(pid, bool) or not isinstance(pid, int) or pid <= 1:
        return False
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except PermissionError:
        return True
    return True


def own_live_pid(pid):
    # Alive AND signalable by this user: a pid recycled by someone else's process is not our companion.
    if isinstance(pid, bool) or not isinstance(pid, int) or pid <= 1:
        return False
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except OSError:
        return False
    return True


def connect_record(root):
    # connect.json (hmd app connect), believed only when it is ours and nobody else can write it; None otherwise
    return STATE.read_json(root, APP_REL, "connect.json", READ_CAP, forbidden=NOT_SHARED)


def companion_connected(rec):
    # A phone can reach this session right now: connect.json names at least one process,
    # every one of them alive and ours (pid_ui, pid_client).
    if rec is None:
        return False
    pids = [rec[k] for k in ("pid_ui", "pid_client") if k in rec]
    return bool(pids) and all(own_live_pid(p) for p in pids)


def tmux_optin(rec, reg):
    # `hmd app connect --tmux` named this session's pane in connect.json's `tmux` list, and the pane and socket agree with both the
    # SessionStart record and the session's own environment. The pid in an entry only says who was checked then: the entry matches by
    # pane, so the opt-in follows the pane across a Claude Code restart, and own_pane() proves the pane again every time before a key.
    pane, sock = session_tmux()
    entries = rec.get("tmux") if rec is not None else None
    if not pane or not sock or not isinstance(entries, list) or reg.get("tmux_pane") != pane or reg.get("tmux_socket") != sock:
        return False
    return any(isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("pane") == pane and e.get("socket") == sock for e in entries)


def probe(argv):
    # stdout of argv or None: ps and tmux are signals that may be missing, never errors. No shell.
    try:
        done = subprocess.run(argv, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                              stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, timeout=PROBE_TIMEOUT_S)
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    return done.stdout.decode("utf-8", "replace") if done.returncode == 0 else None


def pending_ids(root):
    # Ids of pending records the paired phone wrote, from an inbox only our own tooling can have
    # produced (see SECURITY). Message text is never kept: the wake needs only "is there one" and
    # "have I woken for it".
    raw = STATE.read(root, UI_REL, "inbox.jsonl", MAX_INBOX_READ, forbidden=PRIVATE, dir_forbidden=NOT_SHARED)
    ids = []
    for line in (raw or b"").decode("utf-8", "replace").splitlines():
        try:
            rec = json.loads(line)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if (isinstance(rec, dict) and rec.get("source") == SOURCE and isinstance(rec.get("id"), str)
                and rec["id"] and isinstance(rec.get("text"), str) and rec["text"].strip()):
            ids.append(rec["id"])
    return ids


def newest(marks):
    return dict(sorted(marks.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1])[-LEDGER_CAP:])


class Ledger(object):
    """inbox-wake.json: {"woken": {record id: epoch}, "typed": {record id: epoch}} under an exclusive flock. "woken" is every wake
    (the exit-2 notice and the keystroke alike), so two sessions of one repo can never both wake for the same message. "typed" is
    the keystroke wake alone: the ids a prompt is being typed into the session's own pane for, written BEFORE the keys go in (and
    taken back if they do not), so that bin/heimdall-inbox-deliver's prompt hook -- the first thing the typed prompt runs --
    finds it and archives the message via "tmux" instead of "prompt", which is what the phone's receipts then show. The notice's
    turn is a task-notification nobody typed and marks nothing. The lock file is opened, and the ledger read and replaced,
    through hmd_private_state: a link on the way to the lock is refused (OSError), a link at the ledger is not believed and is
    replaced by the real file, never followed."""

    def __init__(self, root):
        self.root = root
        self.fd = None

    def __enter__(self):
        self.fd = STATE.open_lockfile(self.root, UI_REL, "inbox-wake.lock")
        try:
            fcntl.flock(self.fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        except BaseException:
            os.close(self.fd)
            raise
        return self

    def __exit__(self, *exc):
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            os.close(self.fd)
        return False

    def marks(self, key):
        rec = STATE.read_json(self.root, UI_REL, "inbox-wake.json", READ_CAP, forbidden=PRIVATE) or {}
        m = rec.get(key)
        return m if isinstance(m, dict) else {}

    def save(self, woken, typed):
        body = json.dumps({"woken": newest(woken), "typed": newest(typed)})
        STATE.write(self.root, UI_REL, "inbox-wake.json", body.encode("utf-8"))


def claim(root, ids):
    # The ids this caller is first to wake for (recorded), or [] when another watcher beat it.
    with Ledger(root) as led:
        seen = led.marks("woken")
        fresh = [i for i in ids if i not in seen]
        if fresh:
            now = time.time()
            seen.update({i: now for i in fresh})
            led.save(seen, led.marks("typed"))
    return fresh


def mark_typed(root, ids, typed):
    # Record (typed=True) or take back (False) that a prompt is being typed for these ids (see Ledger): the mark goes in first, so the hook
    # the keys run can never beat it, and comes out again when they did not go in.
    with Ledger(root) as led:
        marks = led.marks("typed")
        for i in ids:
            if typed:
                marks[i] = time.time()
            else:
                marks.pop(i, None)
        led.save(led.marks("woken"), marks)


def session_status(pid):
    base = os.environ.get("HMD_CLAUDE_SESSIONS_DIR") or os.path.join(
        os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR") or os.path.expanduser("~/.claude"), "sessions")
    # Claude Code's own status file, outside the repo: no mode is demanded of it, but a link is not believed.
    rec = STATE.read_json(base, "", "%d.json" % pid, READ_CAP, forbidden=0)
    if rec is None or rec.get("pid") != pid:
        return None
    st = rec.get("status")
    return st if isinstance(st, str) else None


def hold_alive(root):
    st = STATE.stat_file(root, UI_REL, "inbox-waiting")
    return st is not None and 0 <= time.time() - st.st_mtime <= HOLD_FRESH_S


def terminal_of(pid):
    out = (probe(["ps", "-o", "tty=", "-p", str(pid)]) or "").strip()
    if not out or out in ("?", "??", "-") or out.startswith("/") or ".." in out:
        return None
    return os.path.join("/dev", out)


def terminal_read_ago(dev):
    # Seconds since the terminal was last READ (a keystroke taken off the pty), or None.
    try:
        return max(0.0, time.time() - os.stat(dev).st_atime)
    except (OSError, TypeError):
        return None


def ancestors(pid):
    seen, chain = set(), []
    for _ in range(ANCESTOR_HOPS):
        if pid <= 1 or pid in seen:
            break
        seen.add(pid)
        chain.append(pid)
        fields = (probe(["ps", "-o", "ppid=", "-p", str(pid)]) or "").split()
        if not fields or not fields[0].isdigit():
            break
        pid = int(fields[0])
    return chain


def valid_socket(sock):
    # what the first field of $TMUX looks like: an absolute path with no "..", no newline and a sane length
    return isinstance(sock, str) and sock.startswith("/") and ".." not in sock and "\n" not in sock and len(sock) < 512


def session_tmux():
    # (pane, socket) from THIS process's environment, which a hook inherits from claude: the live truth
    # about where the session runs, unlike a file anybody could drop into the repo. "" when absent or
    # malformed -- the pane must be %N and the socket an absolute path with no "..".
    pane = os.environ.get("TMUX_PANE", "")
    tm = os.environ.get("TMUX", "")
    sock = tm.split(",")[0] if tm else ""
    return (pane if PANE_RE.match(pane) else "", sock if valid_socket(sock) else "")


def tmux_argv(sock):
    return ["tmux", "-S", sock] if sock else ["tmux"]


def process_is_ours(pid):
    out = (probe(["ps", "-o", "uid=", "-p", str(pid)]) or "").strip()
    return out.isdigit() and int(out) == os.geteuid()


def socket_is_ours(sock):
    # a unix socket this user owns (os.stat follows a link, so a link to somebody else's socket is theirs)
    try:
        st = os.stat(sock)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return False
    return stat.S_ISSOCK(st.st_mode) and st.st_uid == os.geteuid()


def pane_belongs(pane, sock, pid):
    # tmux itself lists `pane` (on the server at `sock`) with a process that is an ancestor of claude's `pid` and is this user's
    listing = probe(tmux_argv(sock) + ["list-panes", "-a", "-F", "#{pane_id} #{pane_pid}"])
    if listing is None:
        return False
    chain = set(ancestors(pid))
    for line in listing.splitlines():
        fields = line.split()
        if len(fields) == 2 and fields[0] == pane and fields[1].isdigit() and int(fields[1]) in chain:
            return process_is_ours(int(fields[1]))
    return False


def own_pane(reg, pid):
    # True only when the SessionStart record agrees with this session's own environment AND tmux says
    # that pane's process is an ancestor of this claude pid: the pane is provably the one claude runs in.
    pane, sock = session_tmux()
    if not pane or reg.get("tmux_pane") != pane or reg.get("tmux_socket") != sock:
        return False
    return pane_belongs(pane, sock, pid)


def type_prompt():
    # argv = validated pane id + socket + constants; WAKE_PROMPT is literal (-l), no message text, no shell.
    pane, sock = session_tmux()
    base = tmux_argv(sock) + ["send-keys", "-t", pane]
    return bool(pane) and all(probe(argv) is not None for argv in (base + ["-l", WAKE_PROMPT], base + ["Enter"]))


def load_registration(root, pid):
    rec = STATE.read_json(root, WAKE_REL, "%d.json" % pid, READ_CAP, forbidden=PRIVATE)
    return rec if rec is not None and rec.get("pid") == pid else {}


def wake_mode():
    m = os.environ.get("HMD_INBOX_WAKE", "").strip().lower()
    return m if m in ("rewake", "tmux") or m in SWITCHED_OFF else ""


def prune_dead(root):
    for name in STATE.names(root, WAKE_REL):
        m = re.match(r"^([0-9]+)\.(json|lock)$", name)
        if m and not pid_alive(int(m.group(1))):
            STATE.remove(root, WAKE_REL, name)


def cmd_register(root, pid, payload):
    if not attended_session() or wake_mode() in SWITCHED_OFF or not pid_alive(pid):
        return 0
    pane, sock = session_tmux()
    rec = {"pid": pid, "session_id": payload.get("session_id") if isinstance(payload.get("session_id"), str) else "",
           "tty": terminal_of(pid), "registered_at": time.time(), "tmux_pane": pane, "tmux_socket": sock}
    STATE.write(root, WAKE_REL, "%d.json" % pid, json.dumps(rec).encode("utf-8"))
    prune_dead(root)
    return 0


def take_instance_lock(root, pid):
    fd = STATE.open_lockfile(root, WAKE_REL, "%d.lock" % pid)     # OSError = refused: main() exits 0, no wake
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError:
        os.close(fd)
        return None
    return fd


def wake_action(root, pid):
    # "tmux" (typed a prompt into the session's own pane), "rewake" (the caller exits 2) or
    # None (conditions not met this tick). Claims the pending ids before acting, so a second
    # watcher never wakes for them.
    mode = wake_mode()
    if mode in SWITCHED_OFF:
        return None
    ids = pending_ids(root)
    if not ids or session_status(pid) == "busy" or hold_alive(root):
        return None
    conn = connect_record(root)
    if not companion_connected(conn):
        return None
    reg = load_registration(root, pid)
    dev = reg.get("tty") if isinstance(reg.get("tty"), str) else terminal_of(pid)
    read_ago = terminal_read_ago(dev)
    if read_ago is not None and read_ago < TYPING_RECENT_S:
        return None        # somebody is at the keyboard: their prompt carries the message
    quiet = env_float("HMD_INBOX_WAKE_TMUX_QUIET_S", DEFAULT_TMUX_QUIET_S)
    settled = read_ago is None or read_ago >= quiet      # unread for the quiet window: no half-typed draft can be pending
    if mode != "rewake" and not settled and tmux_optin(conn, reg):
        return None        # --tmux: the pane is the delivery path, so a draft's window is waited out (nothing claimed), not answered with the notice
    fresh = claim(root, ids)
    if not fresh:
        return None
    if mode != "rewake" and settled and own_pane(reg, pid):
        mark_typed(root, fresh, True)         # BEFORE the keys, so the prompt hook they run finds it (see Ledger); a refusal ends the tick with no key typed
        if type_prompt():
            return "tmux"
        with contextlib.suppress(OSError):
            mark_typed(root, fresh, False)    # no keys went in: the notice below is this wake, and no delivery by tmux follows it
    return "rewake"


def cmd_watch(root, pid):
    if not attended_session() or wake_mode() in SWITCHED_OFF or not pid_alive(pid):
        return 0
    lock = take_instance_lock(root, pid)
    if lock is None:
        return 0            # a watcher is already armed for this session
    poll_s = max(0.05, env_float("HMD_INBOX_WAKE_POLL_S", DEFAULT_POLL_S))
    deadline = time.time() + env_float("HMD_INBOX_WAKE_MAX_S", DEFAULT_MAX_S)
    while time.time() < deadline and pid_alive(pid):
        if wake_action(root, pid) == "rewake":
            sys.stderr.write(WAKE_NOTICE + "\n")
            return 2
        time.sleep(poll_s)
    return 0


def registered_sessions(root):
    # (pid, registration) of the sessions of this repo that registered at SessionStart: a record this user wrote (0600, reached
    # through no link) naming a process that is alive and signalable by this user
    found = []
    for name in STATE.names(root, WAKE_REL):
        m = re.match(r"^([0-9]+)\.json$", name)
        if m and own_live_pid(int(m.group(1))):
            reg = load_registration(root, int(m.group(1)))
            if reg:
                found.append((int(m.group(1)), reg))
    return found


def refuse(why):
    sys.stderr.write(why + "\n")
    return 1


def cmd_optin(root):
    # See TMUX OPT-IN. A session with THIS process among its descendants is the one asking (connect run inside it) and the only one
    # considered; run from another pane, every registered session of the repo is. Read-only: nothing typed, nothing written.
    if shutil.which("tmux") is None:
        return refuse("tmux was not found on PATH")
    sessions = registered_sessions(root)
    if not sessions:
        return refuse("no Claude Code session of this repo has registered with the wake hook "
                      "(a session registers at SessionStart: start Claude Code in this repo with the hmd hooks on)")
    asking = set(ancestors(os.getpid()))
    pool = [s for s in sessions if s[0] in asking] or sessions
    in_tmux = [(pid, reg) for pid, reg in pool
               if PANE_RE.match(str(reg.get("tmux_pane"))) and valid_socket(reg.get("tmux_socket"))]
    if not in_tmux:
        return refuse("this repo's Claude Code session is not running inside tmux "
                      "(its pane is recorded when it starts: start it from a tmux pane)")
    verified, why = [], ""
    for pid, reg in in_tmux:
        pane, sock = reg["tmux_pane"], reg["tmux_socket"]
        if not socket_is_ours(sock):
            why = "the tmux socket %s is not a socket this user owns" % sock
        elif not pane_belongs(pane, sock, pid):
            why = ("tmux does not list pane %s as this session's own (its process is not an ancestor of Claude Code pid %d, "
                   "or is not this user's)" % (pane, pid))
        else:
            verified.append({"pid": pid, "pane": pane, "socket": sock})
    if not verified:
        return refuse(why)
    print(json.dumps(verified))
    return 0


def cmd_status(root):
    live = 0
    for name in STATE.names(root, WAKE_REL):
        m = re.match(r"^([0-9]+)\.json$", name)
        live += bool(m and pid_alive(int(m.group(1))))
    print(json.dumps({"registered": live, "pending": len(pending_ids(root))}))
    return 0


def main(argv):
    global STATE
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="heimdall-inbox-wake", add_help=True)
    ap.add_argument("mode", choices=("register", "watch", "status", "optin"))
    ap.add_argument("--repo", default=os.environ.get("CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR") or os.getcwd())
    ap.add_argument("--pid", type=int, default=os.getppid())
    try:
        args = ap.parse_args(argv)
    except SystemExit:
        return 0            # argparse exits 2 on a bad argument, and under asyncRewake exit 2 WAKES the model
    root = os.path.abspath(args.repo)
    try:
        STATE = _load_private_state()
        if args.mode == "status":
            return cmd_status(root)
        if args.mode == "optin":
            return cmd_optin(root)
        if args.mode == "register":
            try:
                payload = json.loads(sys.stdin.read(65536) or "{}")
            except ValueError:
                payload = {}
            return cmd_register(root, args.pid, payload if isinstance(payload, dict) else {})
        return cmd_watch(root, args.pid)
    except Exception:
        # a refusal (OSError from hmd_private_state: a link or another account's directory on the way) and a
        # wake-mechanism bug end here alike: nothing was written through a link, nothing wakes, exit 0, no output
        return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
